WEBVTT

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.910
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.710
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.400
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:29.130
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:33.470
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.350
But, with you...

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.430
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:43.020
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.740
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:52.120
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.700
Just to survive!

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.500
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.513 --> 00:00:57.353
Take this moment...

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.040
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.330
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.170
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:08.880
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.010
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.720
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.390
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.560
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.390
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.310
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:38.506
Toujou Masumi. Eh, so that’s him?

00:01:39.407 --> 00:01:40.642
Who is this guy anyway?

00:01:41.142 --> 00:01:47.615
Geez! Toujou Masumi is one of the most widely
regarded young artists these days!

00:01:48.082 --> 00:01:49.450
That’s so awesome…

00:01:50.919 --> 00:01:53.688
…that you’re friends with such a famous artist!

00:01:54.455 --> 00:01:59.727
We were in college together but I never
expected ! to become so famous.

00:02:00.094 --> 00:02:02.063
Were you two really just friends?

00:02:02.864 --> 00:02:04.265
What the heck are you saying, smart mouth!

00:02:04.832 --> 00:02:06.401
Why did you hit me?

00:02:06.401 --> 00:02:08.836
O-Oh, sorry! Your head was in the right spot…

00:02:09.137 --> 00:02:10.905
You do that every time!

00:02:10.538 --> 00:02:11.739
Sorry about that.

00:02:12.273 --> 00:02:13.875
Well then, shall we take a look around?

00:02:14.442 --> 00:02:18.046
It’s also important for a detective to
be able to authenticate works of art.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.384
How beautiful!

00:02:23.785 --> 00:02:27.355
I can’t believe it’s really a painting!
The flowers look so alive!

00:02:27.755 --> 00:02:31.059
Don’t they? His paintings have that sort of effect.

00:02:31.593 --> 00:02:36.531
This style of painting is called photo-realism.
There are many dedicated fans of this genre.

00:02:37.298 --> 00:02:38.266
This way, please.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:44.005
The art exhibit opens tomorrow, but I wanted
to give you all an exclusive sneak peek at it.

00:02:44.272 --> 00:02:48.810
I was quite lucky this time to be able to display
the renowned Toujou Masumi’s works.

00:02:49.177 --> 00:02:53.581
They really are wonderful. I became
a fan the moment I saw them.

00:02:53.915 --> 00:02:55.942
They will definitely appreciate in value.

00:02:56.551 --> 00:02:58.553
I bet that one will be worth more than a million yen.

00:02:58.853 --> 00:03:04.292
In that case, as an art investor, it would be
wise to add them to my collection now.

00:03:04.592 --> 00:03:09.764
Shame on you two!! I genuinely
enjoy Toujou-san’s works.

00:03:09.998 --> 00:03:11.866
You may say that, Matsumoto-san…

00:03:11.933 --> 00:03:14.269
…but I've heard that you are making
quite a profit from this business.

00:03:14.602 --> 00:03:15.803
Who said that?

00:03:15.803 --> 00:03:18.706
But in any case, I don’t intend
to leave them for you guys.

00:03:18.706 --> 00:03:19.607
Same here!

00:03:19.974 --> 00:03:25.079
Now, now. There are plenty here today, so
please take your time and look around.

00:03:28.182 --> 00:03:29.617
Who are they?

00:03:30.285 --> 00:03:33.955
That’s probably the sponsor of tomorrow’s
auction and some of his clients.

00:03:34.222 --> 00:03:35.189
Auction?

00:03:35.723 --> 00:03:41.629
It’s a system where buyers bid on an item
and it’s sold to the highest bidder.

00:03:42.263 --> 00:03:44.499
These paintings really do look
as if they will rise in value.

00:03:44.666 --> 00:03:46.167
I might attend the auction too.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.037
What’re you saying? You’re just a grade-schooler!

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.339
Why is it me again?

00:03:51.372 --> 00:03:53.141
Oh! Sorry, sorry. It’s gotten to be a habit…

00:03:56.511 --> 00:03:59.681
Oh! That’s the view from the train!

00:03:59.914 --> 00:04:01.783
Oh, you’re right! That’s our Megu for you!

00:04:02.083 --> 00:04:04.852
I like this painting of food. It speaks to my heart.

00:04:05.453 --> 00:04:09.023
Wow! It looks so good!

00:04:08.189 --> 00:04:09.557
You’re drooling, Kyuu.

00:04:12.694 --> 00:04:14.862
That’s because it looks so delicious.

00:04:15.346 --> 00:04:15.580
I feel honored…

00:04:16.898 --> 00:04:19.133
That you guys see my art that way.

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:20.335
Really.

00:04:21.135 --> 00:04:22.904
Your work is making quite an impact.

00:04:25.406 --> 00:04:29.210
I wasn’t sure I would continue
painting after the accident.

00:04:30.345 --> 00:04:33.581
But now it’s become second nature
to use my left hand when I paint.

00:04:34.549 --> 00:04:36.951
When I was in college, I was
in a hit-and-run accident.

00:04:37.952 --> 00:04:41.289
A nerve was severed in my right hand,
which is my dominant hand.

00:04:41.622 --> 00:04:44.625
Even after that, to be able to create
such wonderful paintings…

00:04:44.792 --> 00:04:46.994
You must be really talented, Toujou-san!

00:04:48.696 --> 00:04:51.299
It’s all thanks to her encouragement.

00:04:51.866 --> 00:04:53.067
Don’t say something like that…

00:04:54.502 --> 00:04:56.137
Sorry for intruding at such a busy time.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.373
It’s okay, the preparations are almost over.

00:04:58.773 --> 00:05:03.111
Was this the model for the painting that’s
in the gallery downstairs, Toujou-kun?

00:05:03.111 --> 00:05:06.714
Eh? But these flowers are a bit
different from the painting.

00:05:06.948 --> 00:05:07.515
Oh, is that right?

00:05:07.882 --> 00:05:12.687
You don’t get it, Megu! Artists don’t
copy exactly what they see.

00:05:13.054 --> 00:05:16.424
Artists make their paintings look more enchanting
and enticing than the original model.

00:05:16.591 --> 00:05:21.229
So the model and the painting don’t
necessarily have to look the same.

00:05:21.562 --> 00:05:22.530
Isn’t that right, Toujou-san?

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.165
No

00:05:24.165 --> 00:05:28.236
Oh, no, I mean that painting actually
depicts a different set of sunflowers.

00:05:28.669 --> 00:05:32.373
I'm surprised you noticed the difference.
They are very similar.

00:05:34.041 --> 00:05:37.078
That’s Megu for you! Her observation
skills are perfect!

00:05:39.447 --> 00:05:42.150
Toujou-san, do you like jigsaw puzzles?

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.252
It looks so hard!

00:05:44.452 --> 00:05:45.453
Let me see!

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.622
Wow! It’s pure white!

00:05:48.623 --> 00:05:53.261
For a jigsaw puzzle without a picture, you
can only rely on the shape of the pieces.

00:05:53.628 --> 00:05:57.398
This type is called a "White Puzzle” and
it’s the most difficult of all puzzles.

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:01.736
I started it just to kill time, but
I ended up getting hooked!

00:06:02.437 --> 00:06:04.071
How many pieces are there?

00:06:04.906 --> 00:06:06.941
I believe it was 5000 pieces.

00:06:06.941 --> 00:06:08.142
5000 pieces?

00:06:08.443 --> 00:06:11.012
Amazing! I've never seen one like that!

00:06:11.245 --> 00:06:14.849
And what you did call it? "White
Puzzle“? What kind is that?

00:06:15.049 --> 00:06:16.784
H-hey, watch out, Kinta!

00:06:18.085 --> 00:06:19.754
Oh, no!

00:06:19.754 --> 00:06:21.022
You’ve done it now.

00:06:21.289 --> 00:06:24.091
How many days do you think it
took to complete this thing?

00:06:24.392 --> 00:06:25.893
Oh, my! You guys!

00:06:25.893 --> 00:06:27.028
Ah, it’s okay!

00:06:27.562 --> 00:06:30.064
I can fix it in no time, Kinta-kun.

00:06:30.465 --> 00:06:32.633
Geez, Kinta! You’re so careless!

00:06:33.468 --> 00:06:35.903
Uhm, let me see…

00:06:42.143 --> 00:06:43.911
It can’t be…

00:06:49.116 --> 00:06:50.785
You haven’t changed a bit.

00:06:51.219 --> 00:06:55.056
You haven’t either. Although, you
are a lot more famous now…

00:06:56.991 --> 00:06:58.659
They were all wonderful paintings.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.162
You have a splendid talent!

00:07:01.596 --> 00:07:02.797
Talent, eh?

00:07:03.764 --> 00:07:06.467
In my case it might be a little different…

00:07:06.467 --> 00:07:08.002
Eh?

00:07:08.002 --> 00:07:09.470
Didn’t you hear what Kinta-kun said?

00:07:10.304 --> 00:07:14.442
“Artists make their paintings look more enchanting
and enticing than the original model."

00:07:14.742 --> 00:07:16.143
But in my case…

00:07:17.245 --> 00:07:17.979
Toujou-kun…

00:07:20.548 --> 00:07:24.151
Hey! How about some lunch?

00:07:24.285 --> 00:07:25.853
Alright!

00:07:26.988 --> 00:07:28.222
Lunch, lunch!

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:32.627
Lunch with a popular artist! Who would’ve thought!

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.529
You’re just saying that because
you’re hungry, aren’t you?

00:07:37.365 --> 00:07:39.433
There will be some wonderful
things to bid on tomorrow.

00:07:39.433 --> 00:07:41.102
Thank you very much.

00:07:42.103 --> 00:07:43.504
I have great expectations for them.

00:07:45.139 --> 00:07:46.874
Can’t let Matsumoto-san get
all the great deals, can we?

00:07:50.144 --> 00:07:51.445
Toujou-san?

00:07:52.079 --> 00:07:53.247
What’s wrong?

00:07:54.048 --> 00:07:56.984
Oh, I just remembered that I
have another engagement.

00:07:57.084 --> 00:07:58.786
Please go ahead and eat without me.

00:08:00.821 --> 00:08:03.558
Toujou-kun, are you not feeling well?

00:08:03.758 --> 00:08:06.594
Oh, it’s nothing. I'll be back in no time. Later.

00:08:11.065 --> 00:08:12.934
I'm full!

00:08:13.768 --> 00:08:15.703
Toujou-san’s taking a lot of time…

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:18.205
He said he would come back right away…

00:08:18.573 --> 00:08:21.275
Maybe he got into a quarrel about the auction?

00:08:21.576 --> 00:08:22.476
What do you mean?

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:27.081
Selling art works is a delicate matter;
many things can come up.

00:08:27.448 --> 00:08:32.253
Come to think of it, Toujou-san had a strange
expression when he saw those four people.

00:08:33.154 --> 00:08:36.457
I'll go take a look. You guys stay here.

00:08:36.757 --> 00:08:37.959
Katagiri-Sensei!

00:08:39.927 --> 00:08:41.128
I'll go with you!

00:08:42.029 --> 00:08:42.930
Toujou-kun?

00:08:50.972 --> 00:08:53.808
Toujou-kun? Are you here?

00:08:54.442 --> 00:08:55.610
Toujou-san?

00:09:17.431 --> 00:09:18.399
Toujou-kun!

00:09:20.267 --> 00:09:23.004
Katagiri-Sensei, how is he?

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:33.114
That can’t be! He was with
us just a few minutes ago!

00:09:33.514 --> 00:09:35.750
Calm down, Minami-san!

00:09:38.252 --> 00:09:41.255
Calm yourself, Minami-san…

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:48.529
Everyone! Until the police arrive, we
from DDS will investigate this case.

00:09:49.597 --> 00:09:51.766
Please give me your full cooperation.

00:09:52.066 --> 00:09:54.869
Everyone! Please stay inside the hotel!

00:09:55.903 --> 00:10:01.175
Please tell me as accurate as possible what
you were doing a few minutes ago.

00:10:02.076 --> 00:10:06.080
Umm, like I said before… What
were you doing then?

00:10:08.315 --> 00:10:12.253
Grandpa, listen, that time… Uhm, weren’t we…

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.722
What was I going to say?

00:10:15.456 --> 00:10:18.392
Please take your time and try to remember.

00:10:18.926 --> 00:10:22.363
What’s this about? Why did you call only us in here?

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:27.501
I want to ask you what you were doing
during the last thirty minutes.

00:10:28.102 --> 00:10:31.906
Why are you just asking us? There
were other people there too!

00:10:32.206 --> 00:10:33.874
The hotel staff as well!

00:10:33.874 --> 00:10:36.711
Isn't it possible that the crime was committed
by somebody who came in from outside?

00:10:38.679 --> 00:10:43.651
Everyone, other than you four, had a solid alibi.

00:10:44.018 --> 00:10:47.188
We’ve confirmed that none of the restaurant
employees went outside.

00:10:47.555 --> 00:10:50.491
We’ve also checked all the security
cameras in the building.

00:10:50.524 --> 00:10:53.394
…but nobody entered the building during that time.

00:10:53.861 --> 00:10:57.164
Are you trying to say that the
culprit is one of us then?

00:10:57.331 --> 00:10:59.934
Are you seriously suspecting us?

00:11:00.401 --> 00:11:04.238
We aren’t saying that. We just
want to confirm your alibis.

00:11:04.405 --> 00:11:08.075
No way… I don’t even know what
Toujou-Sensei looks like!

00:11:08.309 --> 00:11:13.247
I just came down here from Hokkaido and
I've never met Toujou-Sensei either.

00:11:13.247 --> 00:11:16.550
As for me, I just arrived here from Hakata!

00:11:16.951 --> 00:11:18.219
And I have no reason to kill him!

00:11:18.986 --> 00:11:22.423
To begin with, this guy here is the
only one who knew Toujou-san!

00:11:22.523 --> 00:11:26.427
But why would I kill my business partner?

00:11:26.694 --> 00:11:28.829
My living depends on this business!

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:30.865
Don’t talk nonsense!

00:11:30.865 --> 00:11:34.902
In any case, we need your alibis
to prove you innocent!

00:11:38.606 --> 00:11:44.245
I was in my office getting ready for
tomorrow’s auction the whole time.

00:11:44.912 --> 00:11:45.679
It’s the truth!

00:11:46.313 --> 00:11:49.483
After I left Orita-san and the others,
I was taking a nap in my room.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:51.519
Until somebody wake me up, that is!

00:11:52.353 --> 00:11:54.522
I was making some phone calls in my room.

00:11:54.755 --> 00:11:57.691
This is the record of the calls. You can see it, right?

00:11:58.592 --> 00:12:00.227
I was drinking beer in my room.

00:12:00.861 --> 00:12:03.564
Huh!? What’s with that look? Do you suspect me?

00:12:03.864 --> 00:12:04.965
What’s that, you…!

00:12:05.666 --> 00:12:07.001
Thank you very much.

00:12:07.468 --> 00:12:10.404
I'd like to ask everyone to wait
here for a little while longer.

00:12:21.816 --> 00:12:25.052
None of them had a solid alibi…

00:12:25.419 --> 00:12:28.656
However, Toujou-san seemed
startled when he saw them.

00:12:28.956 --> 00:12:31.592
I think Orita-san, the owner of
gallery, is the most suspicious.

00:12:32.259 --> 00:12:35.963
An artist’s work usually appreciates
in value after his death.

00:12:37.064 --> 00:12:41.435
In my opinion, I don’t like that
arrogant old man Takase!

00:12:42.336 --> 00:12:43.537
What do you think, Kyuu-kun?

00:12:44.004 --> 00:12:49.009
It’s unusual for a suspect to kill someone
they don’t even know, but…

00:12:50.311 --> 00:12:53.013
I'm still suspicions of those four…

00:12:54.582 --> 00:12:56.150
The murder weapon was left at the scene.

00:12:56.317 --> 00:12:58.552
The culprit didn’t even attempt
to get rid of the evidence.

00:12:59.186 --> 00:13:03.023
Based on that, this murder doesn’t
seem to have been planned.

00:13:03.524 --> 00:13:04.291
I agree.

00:13:04.525 --> 00:13:07.595
If that’s the case, there must have been
some kind of unplanned motive.

00:13:08.062 --> 00:13:09.330
Let’s try to find out what that was.

00:13:09.563 --> 00:13:10.497
Please hold on!

00:13:12.166 --> 00:13:12.766
Megu?

00:13:13.467 --> 00:13:17.972
Your friend was murdered, Katagiri-Sensei!

00:13:18.772 --> 00:13:20.074
Aren’t you sad at all?

00:13:21.709 --> 00:13:26.146
Regardless, let’s inspect the crime scene once more.

00:13:26.847 --> 00:13:28.482
You’re so cold, Sensei!

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:32.853
We are all members of DDS.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.798
Let’s go back to the crime scene, Megu.

00:13:45.266 --> 00:13:49.169
W-well then, let’s continue interrogating
those four, Kazuma!

00:13:49.169 --> 00:13:50.004
Ah, yes.

00:13:59.313 --> 00:13:59.914
Megu?

00:14:00.681 --> 00:14:02.182
It’s just like Sensei said…

00:14:03.284 --> 00:14:07.588
How can a case be solved when
the detective is upset?

00:14:08.389 --> 00:14:12.927
But, if I can’t get sad when my friend dies…

00:14:14.194 --> 00:14:16.697
…I'd rather not be a detective…

00:14:17.665 --> 00:14:18.265
It’s alright.

00:14:20.968 --> 00:14:25.105
Of course you’d be sad if your friend died.

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:27.408
Your feelings aren’t wrong, Megu.

00:14:28.309 --> 00:14:31.779
And I think Shino-san feels the same too.

00:14:31.779 --> 00:14:33.714
Kyuu…

00:14:33.714 --> 00:14:34.248
Let’s go!

00:14:42.323 --> 00:14:42.990
Forgive me…

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:47.428
You guys!

00:14:49.296 --> 00:14:50.764
Katagiri-Sensei…

00:14:52.933 --> 00:14:54.034
I'm sorry.

00:14:58.172 --> 00:14:59.139
What’s this?

00:14:59.807 --> 00:15:02.309
They were in Toujou-kun’s pocket.

00:15:02.543 --> 00:15:07.581
Eh? But the puzzle was complete when we last saw it!

00:15:08.082 --> 00:15:11.151
That means he put them in his
pocket just before he died?

00:15:11.785 --> 00:15:12.553
That means.…

00:15:13.187 --> 00:15:14.321
That’s right.

00:15:14.321 --> 00:15:22.529
He was unable to find anything to write with so he
left a dying message with these puzzle pieces.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:26.200
Then if we put the pieces together
they might form words!

00:15:26.333 --> 00:15:27.868
Could it be the murderer’s name?

00:15:28.235 --> 00:15:28.902
Let’s try!

00:15:33.807 --> 00:15:34.942
This is all of them.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.712
They seem to be grouped in some way, but…

00:15:39.146 --> 00:15:40.781
It doesn’t seem like it’s a word…

00:15:40.948 --> 00:15:46.053
But Toujou-kun used the last of his energy
to put these pieces in his pocket.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:48.989
There must be something that
will point out the culprit.

00:15:49.523 --> 00:15:51.759
I've realized something.

00:15:56.263 --> 00:16:00.034
This painting depicts the flowers
in the lobby of this hotel.

00:16:03.504 --> 00:16:04.304
What?

00:16:04.605 --> 00:16:06.173
Are you sure, Minami-san?

00:16:06.774 --> 00:16:10.778
I'm pretty sure. Each and every
petal is exactly the same.

00:16:11.445 --> 00:16:14.014
He didn’t tell me that he painted it in the hotel lobby.

00:16:15.082 --> 00:16:17.618
There’s probably only one explanation for that.

00:16:18.352 --> 00:16:21.622
To Toujou-san, painting a flower
right in front of him…

00:16:21.722 --> 00:16:24.925
…and painting a flower that he once
glanced at was the same thing.

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:27.461
Toujou-san probably had…

00:16:28.062 --> 00:16:29.963
…the same ability as Megu!

00:16:30.931 --> 00:16:32.866
He had a photographic memory!

00:16:33.233 --> 00:16:38.272
And, he probably realized that Megu
has the same ability as he did.

00:16:39.873 --> 00:16:46.013
When Kinta messed up the puzzle, he just laughed
and said that he could fix it in no time.

00:16:46.713 --> 00:16:50.017
What’s more, he was staring at Megu
when she was fixing the puzzle.

00:16:52.486 --> 00:16:57.591
That’s it! When he saw those four
his expression changed suddenly.

00:16:58.192 --> 00:17:05.632
That probably was because he saw one
of them once before and didn’t forget
because of his photographic memory!

00:17:06.533 --> 00:17:10.104
That means the culprit and Toujou-san
barely knew each other.

00:17:10.537 --> 00:17:15.409
If he didn’t know the culprit’s name,
what kind of message did he leave?

00:17:16.009 --> 00:17:20.848
In his last moments, Toujou-kun
entrusted everything to you…

00:17:21.315 --> 00:17:25.252
…believing you could reassemble the puzzle
because you have that same ability.

00:17:25.252 --> 00:17:25.953
The floor!

00:17:26.186 --> 00:17:28.789
Can you put the pieces that are scattered
on the floor together, Megu?

00:17:29.389 --> 00:17:31.592
I've already seen the completed form, so…

00:17:32.559 --> 00:17:34.161
I'm sure I can!

00:17:44.873 --> 00:17:47.476
Thank you for your assistance, DDS.

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:50.278
I'm Mara from the prefectural police department.

00:17:50.946 --> 00:17:53.215
By the way, what is that girl doing?

00:17:57.486 --> 00:18:00.255
After keeping us here for so long,
what do you want with us now?

00:18:00.589 --> 00:18:03.291
Shame on you for suspecting us!

00:18:03.825 --> 00:18:07.396
Please remain here until your alibis are confirmed.

00:18:07.663 --> 00:18:09.364
How much longer do we have to wait?

00:18:09.598 --> 00:18:11.466
We’re investigating it as fast as we can.

00:18:11.933 --> 00:18:16.438
In any case, please hurry it up! I have
to notify everyone concerned.

00:18:17.339 --> 00:18:19.808
What in the world are you guys
doing at a time like this?

00:18:20.776 --> 00:18:21.843
A puzzle?

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:24.413
I don’t care if it’s DDS or not…

00:18:24.413 --> 00:18:32.354
Everyone! This jigsaw puzzle
is the victim’s dying message.

00:18:33.555 --> 00:18:34.489
What did you say?

00:18:34.990 --> 00:18:39.828
When this puzzle is completed, it
will indicate who the culprit is.

00:18:40.796 --> 00:18:41.630
Nonsense!

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:44.766
How can the culprit be determined
by a thing like that!?

00:18:44.933 --> 00:18:47.035
Of course you’ll provide us with a
reasonable explanation, right?

00:18:47.869 --> 00:18:49.004
There are three hints!

00:18:50.105 --> 00:18:53.709
The first one is the fact that Toujou-san
had a photographic memory.

00:18:53.775 --> 00:18:54.776
Photographic?

00:18:55.077 --> 00:18:56.078
What the heck is that?

00:18:56.411 --> 00:19:00.115
The ability to remember anything
that he’s seen before.

00:19:01.016 --> 00:19:03.852
Toujou-san had that ability.

00:19:04.486 --> 00:19:05.153
Could it be…?

00:19:05.387 --> 00:19:07.189
I've never heard of that kind of ability before.

00:19:07.456 --> 00:19:09.357
And secondly…

00:19:10.092 --> 00:19:12.794
Toujou-san didn’t know the murderer’s name.

00:19:13.395 --> 00:19:15.297
How do you know that?

00:19:15.664 --> 00:19:17.265
Yeah, what’s the basis for that?

00:19:17.766 --> 00:19:23.505
These are jigsaw puzzle pieces that
were in Toujou-san’s pocket.

00:19:23.705 --> 00:19:28.176
We put them together, but they didn’t become
any Japanese or alphabet word.

00:19:29.111 --> 00:19:31.313
Toujou-san didn’t know the murderer’s name…

00:19:32.114 --> 00:19:35.984
…so he couldn’t leave the murderer’s
name as his dying message.

00:19:36.585 --> 00:19:39.154
So what type of message are you saying he left?

00:19:39.354 --> 00:19:40.155
Thirdly…

00:19:40.555 --> 00:19:43.391
The fact that Toujou-san is an artistic genius!

00:19:43.992 --> 00:19:46.695
I'm done! The puzzle is complete!

00:19:47.295 --> 00:19:51.733
Everyone! This is Toujou-san’s dying message!

00:19:55.203 --> 00:19:57.105
What’s that supposed to tell us?

00:19:57.172 --> 00:19:58.673
I don’t get it.

00:19:59.641 --> 00:20:00.842
There’s only one answer!

00:20:01.610 --> 00:20:02.711
Kinta! Kazuma!

00:20:02.944 --> 00:20:03.612
Alright!

00:20:03.845 --> 00:20:05.347
We’re all set!

00:20:06.948 --> 00:20:12.354
In his last moments, Toujou-san created the culprit’s
portrait by taking out puzzle pieces.

00:20:12.487 --> 00:20:13.488
That’s enough joking around!

00:20:13.989 --> 00:20:15.590
Give us a reasonable explanation!

00:20:16.091 --> 00:20:17.592
There’s no more need to explain!

00:20:17.692 --> 00:20:19.928
All that’s left is to break apart this puzzle!

00:20:47.155 --> 00:20:51.860
The person who murdered
Toujou Masumi-san is you!

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:53.161
Yamazaki-san!

00:20:55.197 --> 00:20:56.064
Stop it!

00:20:57.332 --> 00:20:58.934
Don’t look at me like that!

00:21:01.069 --> 00:21:02.771
Don’t look at me!

00:21:10.812 --> 00:21:13.081
Nice to meet you, Toujou-Sensei.

00:21:13.515 --> 00:21:15.750
All of your pictures are quite splendid!

00:21:16.184 --> 00:21:19.487
I'd like to invest in them at any cost.

00:21:21.356 --> 00:21:24.059
I was in an accident 10 years ago.

00:21:25.427 --> 00:21:30.498
I clearly remember the red sports
car that you were driving…

00:21:31.132 --> 00:21:34.569
…and even the green sweater that
you were wearing that day.

00:21:37.138 --> 00:21:38.473
Toujou-Sensei…

00:21:40.008 --> 00:21:42.611
It was raining hard that day…

00:21:42.911 --> 00:21:47.282
I'm sure the visibility was very
poor when you were driving.

00:21:52.787 --> 00:21:56.157
I've been incapable of using my
right hand since the accident.

00:22:00.729 --> 00:22:05.567
I was scared! I didn’t know what
to do and when I realized…

00:22:14.175 --> 00:22:15.176
Yamazaki-san.

00:22:18.914 --> 00:22:22.884
What do you think he was going to say to you?

00:22:23.985 --> 00:22:26.655
"I've been incapable of using my right hand…"

00:22:26.655 --> 00:22:28.390
"But"

00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:29.491
After that, probably…

00:22:29.925 --> 00:22:32.027
“But I don’t hold a grudge against you."

00:22:32.994 --> 00:22:34.729
I think that’s what he was about to say.

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:40.068
If he wasn’t intending to say that, he
wouldn’t have met with you alone.

00:22:40.735 --> 00:22:42.604
Toujou-kun is that kind of person.

00:22:43.872 --> 00:22:45.540
Oh no…

00:22:53.114 --> 00:22:54.716
Thank you, Minami-san.

00:22:55.917 --> 00:23:01.690
In the end, he was able to leave a message because
he met a person with the same ability.

00:23:02.223 --> 00:23:03.425
Katagiri-Sensei…

00:23:03.725 --> 00:23:07.362
Sensei, this is the picture that Toujou-san
was painting in his studio…

00:23:08.463 --> 00:23:10.465
Doesn’t it kind of look like you?

00:23:12.067 --> 00:23:16.304
”Artists make their paintings look more enchanting
and enticing than the original model."

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:47.070
Unable to cry in front of you, I'm whistling instead.

00:23:49.780 --> 00:24:01.630
Saying "I'll always be beside you" without saying a single word.

00:24:01.630 --> 00:24:08.720
My loving heart is overflowing; those sad thoughts...

00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:14.350
are like things that fade away unnoticed in mid-air.

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:20.560
And again, with a mighty smile of relief...

00:24:20.690 --> 00:24:26.110
I will see you off.

00:24:26.360 --> 00:24:35.950
Goodbye and thank you.

00:24:37.353 --> 00:24:39.989
The mysterious bishounen genius, Amakusa Ryuu.

00:24:40.222 --> 00:24:44.126
On our way to DDS’s special
case on Kirisaki Island…

00:24:44.360 --> 00:24:46.228
…Class Q has a fateful encounter with him.

00:24:46.562 --> 00:24:48.731
Just who in the world is he?

00:24:48.731 --> 00:24:53.369
And now the tragedy of Kirisaki Island will be revealed…

00:24:53.369 --> 00:24:54.670
There’s only one answer!

00:24:57.139 --> 00:24:59.775
This time we’ll practice using photographic memory!

00:24:59.942 --> 00:25:02.311
Memorize the numbers that will appear in a flash.

00:25:03.078 --> 00:25:05.047
How did you do? Did you get all them all?

00:25:05.414 --> 00:25:07.349
It works if you view them as one picture!

00:25:07.650 --> 00:25:08.584
Well then, once more!

00:25:09.318 --> 00:25:10.085
Did you get them?
